Retro Album Cover
AI prompt:
Create a dreamy 1980s retro album cover with a long summer highway and vintage cars. Add a pink convertible in the foreground with palm trees and a giant glowing pink sun. Use bright pink purple and blue colors with neon lights and a dreamy summer night drive vibe. 
Make it look cute nostalgic and cinematic.
Vocab List:
1.Value-The bright colors make the picture pop and set a fun mood. The sunset reminds me of the end of a movie.
2.Space-The long highway makes it feel like you're there in the car with the girl and seeing things from her point of view.
3.Unity-The colors and objects work together even though there is a lot going on and the picture looks a little unrealistic.
4.Balance-The picture feels balanced because there are cars on the road and palm trees on both sides with objects spread throughout the scene.
5.Rhythm-The palm trees lead inward toward the sun. They get smaller as they go farther away and guide your eyes toward the center of the picture.
Reflection:
When I look at my picture the first thing I notice is the sun because it’s right in the center and it’s a different color than all the pink purple and blue around it. I also notice the car and the girl inside because she looks like she’s having a good time. 
It makes me feel like I want to be there with her and experience that moment. The whole picture gives me the feeling of a perfect summer evening. Like I said before it reminds me of the end of a movie where everything is finally okay and you feel like everything is going to work out. I really like how the colors make everything look dreamy and kind of unreal but in a good way. 
The highway makes it feel like you’re actually there in the car looking ahead at the sunset. The palm trees also lead your eyes toward the sun and get smaller the farther away they are. I think that makes the picture look more realistic even though the colors are very bright. The picture also feels balanced because there are palm trees on both sides and cars on the road. Even though there is a lot going on everything fits together. Overall this picture makes me feel happy and hopeful. It gives me this feeling of enlightenment and makes me wish I could experience a moment like that myself.
